    the channel-invariant (both dimensionless), not the ABSOLUTE normalization that selects among
    `{1, 3/2}`. That datum lives one rung up, in the running/transmutation scale. -/
theorem temperings_disagree : doublingTempered ≠ ratioTempered := by
  rw [doublingTempered_eq, ratioTempered_eq]; norm_num

/-- ★★ BOTH ADMISSIBLE TEMPERINGS CARRY THE OVERSHOOT DOWN: both are strictly below the raw
    overshooting census `gatherIsoSpinCensus = 4`. Each is a genuine REDUCTION of the raw census, as
    the predecessor's overshoot demands. -/
theorem temperings_reduce_overshoot :
    ratioTempered < gatherIsoSpinCensus ∧ doublingTempered < gatherIsoSpinCensus := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [ratioTempered_eq, gatherIsoSpinCensus_eq]; norm_num
  · rw [doublingTempered_eq, gatherIsoSpinCensus_eq]; norm_num

/-- ★★ BOTH ADMISSIBLE TEMPERINGS GIVE A POSITIVE NET RUNNING CENSUS: `0 < netIsoDepth ratioTempered`
    (`= 1/2`) and `0 < netIsoDepth doublingTempered` (`= 1`). UNLIKE the raw census (`naive_netIso_
    negative`, predecessor: `netIsoDepth 4 = −2 < 0`), both temperings keep the coupling running the
    physical direction — both are genuine candidates. -/
theorem temperings_net_positive :
    (0 : Cut) < netIsoDepth ratioTempered ∧ (0 : Cut) < netIsoDepth doublingTempered := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · unfold netIsoDepth; rw [isoDepth_eq, ratioTempered_eq]; norm_num
  · unfold netIsoDepth; rw [isoDepth_eq, doublingTempered_eq]; norm_num

/-! ## (E) W8 NON-VACUITY WITH TEETH. -/

/-- ★ W8 — THE RATIO TEMPERING GENUINELY REDUCES THE RAW CENSUS: `ratioTempered ≠ gatherIsoSpinCensus`
    (`3/2 ≠ 4`). Not a vacuous no-op. -/
theorem ratioTempered_ne_raw : ratioTempered ≠ gatherIsoSpinCensus := by
  rw [ratioTempered_eq, gatherIsoSpinCensus_eq]; norm_num

/-- ★ W8 — THE DOUBLING TEMPERING GENUINELY REDUCES THE RAW CENSUS: `doublingTempered ≠
    gatherIsoSpinCensus` (`1 ≠ 4`). -/
theorem doublingTempered_ne_raw : doublingTempered ≠ gatherIsoSpinCensus := by
  rw [doublingTempered_eq, gatherIsoSpinCensus_eq]; norm_num

/-- ★ W8 — THE DOUBLING TEMPERING IS GENUINELY INTERIOR, NOT THE BOUNDARY: `doublingTempered ≠
    isoDepth` (`1 ≠ 2`). The two admissible candidates and the boundary halving are three genuinely
    different values. -/
theorem doublingTempered_ne_isoDepth : doublingTempered ≠ isoDepth := by
  rw [doublingTempered_eq, isoDepth_eq]; norm_num

/-! ## (F) THE CAPSTONE — welded, non-hollow. -/

/-- ★★★ THE ANTI-SCREENING TEMPERING CEILING (arc-D remainder, welded landing). The route-finder for
    the adjoint→fundamental tempering the predecessor named — and the exact structural ceiling it
    uncovers:

    (1) THE TWO CENSUS-NATIVE TEMPERING VALUES: the ratio tempering (banked `3:8`) gives
        `ratioTempered = 3/2` (`ratioTempered_eq`); the doubling tempering (banked doubling square)
        gives `doublingTempered = 1` (`doublingTempered_eq`);
    (2) BOTH ADMISSIBLE: `0 < ratioTempered < isoDepth` (`ratioTempered_admissible`) and
        `0 < doublingTempered < isoDepth` (`doublingTempered_admissible`) — both FIX the predecessor's
        inadmissibility, landing strictly inside the banked open range;
    (3) ★ THE CEILING (under-determination): the two admissible temperings DISAGREE — `doublingTempered
        ≠ ratioTempered` (`temperings_disagree`); admissibility (which excludes the raw census `4` and
        the boundary halving `halvingReduced = isoDepth`, `halvingReduced_not_admissible`) is NECESSARY
        but NOT SUFFICIENT to pin the point. The census layer under-determines `s`;
    (4) BOTH ARE GENUINE CANDIDATES: both carry the overshoot down (`temperings_reduce_overshoot`) and
        both give a positive net running census (`temperings_net_positive`);
    (5) TEETH: both genuinely reduce the raw census (`ratioTempered_ne_raw`, `doublingTempered_ne_raw`);
        the interior candidate is genuinely not the boundary (`doublingTempered_ne_isoDepth`).

    Statable from no single conjunct alone (non-hollow). ⚠ HONEST GRADE: (1)–(5) THEOREM-EXACT now
    (closed reals / exact inequalities of `Cut`, no error bar). ROUTE-NOT-YET-FOUND (NEVER asserted /
    NEVER fitted): the SELECTION of the interior magnitude `s ∈ (0, isoDepth)` among the admissible
    census candidates `{1, 3/2}` — the ABSOLUTE cross-normalization the census layer cannot supply and
    the running/transmutation scale (one rung up) must; handed to the ONE directed successor. The
    measured `1/α(0)` / `sin²θ_W` are REMOVABLE PROSE ONLY; no empirical number in any proof; no value
    chosen by where a measured value sits (the fit value `≈ 1.90` is named only to be EXCLUDED). -/
theorem antiScreeningTemperingCeiling_landing :
    -- (1) the two census-native tempering values
    ratioTempered = 3 / 2
    ∧ doublingTempered = 1
    -- (2) both admissible (strictly interior to the banked open range)
    ∧ ((0 : Cut) < ratioTempered ∧ ratioTempered < isoDepth)
    ∧ ((0 : Cut) < doublingTempered ∧ doublingTempered < isoDepth)
    -- (3) the ceiling: the two admissible temperings DISAGREE; the halving is the excluded boundary
    ∧ doublingTempered ≠ ratioTempered
    ∧ halvingReduced = isoDepth
    ∧ ¬ ((0 : Cut) < halvingReduced ∧ halvingReduced < isoDepth)
    -- (4) both are genuine candidates: reduce the overshoot, keep the net census positive
    ∧ (ratioTempered < gatherIsoSpinCensus ∧ doublingTempered < gatherIsoSpinCensus)
    ∧ ((0 : Cut) < netIsoDepth ratioTempered ∧ (0 : Cut) < netIsoDepth doublingTempered)
    -- (5) teeth
    ∧ ratioTempered ≠ gatherIsoSpinCensus
    ∧ doublingTempered ≠ gatherIsoSpinCensus
    ∧ doublingTempered ≠ isoDepth :=
  ⟨ratioTempered_eq,
   doublingTempered_eq,
   ratioTempered_admissible,
   doublingTempered_admissible,
   temperings_disagree,
   halvingReduced_eq,
   halvingReduced_not_admissible,
   temperings_reduce_overshoot,
   temperings_net_positive,
   ratioTempered_ne_raw,
   doublingTempered_ne_raw,
   doublingTempered_ne_isoDepth⟩

